Convert phylogenetic trees between Newick, extended Newick, NEXUS, PhyloXML, and NeXML.

## Steps

1. Select `Trees` in the navigation rail {% ref id="A" /%}. On phones, open `More`, then select `Trees`.
2. Open `Convert tree formats` from the tool picker {% ref id="B" /%}: the tool list on wide windows, or the tool name at the top of the page on phones.
3. Add the tree files {% ref id="C" /%} with `Browse files`, `Browse folder`, or `Open archive`. SEGUI searches a folder and its subfolders for tree files, plain or gzipped. See [file input](/docs/gui-usage/intro/#file-input) for mobile options.
4. Select the input format. `Auto` detects the format of each file.
5. Select `Browse` under `Select output directory` to choose the output folder. On phones and tablets, enter a `Directory name` instead; SEGUI saves it in the app's own folder.
6. Select the output format and options. See [Output options](#output-options).
7. Select the run button {% ref id="D" /%}, labeled `Convert`, to start the task.

## Output options

| Option               | Description                                                       |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Strip annotations    | Drop bracket annotations and comments, such as BEAST metadata      |
| Skip TRANSLATE block | Write NEXUS trees with taxon names instead of numbers              |
| Compress with gzip   | Write gzipped output files                                         |

Output files keep the input name with the extension of the output format: `.nwk`, `.enwk`, `.nex`, `.phyloxml`, or `.nexml`. For example, `species.nwk` converted to NEXUS becomes `species.nex`. The app also writes a `report.json` that records the run.

See the [CLI guide](/docs/cli-usage/tree-convert/) for examples of each format.
